(EDRs) installed in cars from Oct 2029.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/new-car-safety-rules-rear-crash-tests-from-2029-to-prevent-fire-immobilisers-from-2027/articleshow/135154655.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/new-car-safety-rules-rear-crash-tests-from-2029-to-prevent-fire-immobilisers-from-2027/articleshow/135154655.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:53:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135154707,imgsize-74548.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Arms training case: US mercenary VanDyke, 6 Ukrainians to remain abroad till Feb 24]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/arms-training-case-us-mercenary-vandyke-6-ukrainians-to-remain-abroad-till-feb-24/articleshow/135154247.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154247.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[VanDyke attended the court hearing Friday and sought the release of his seized personal articles. The seven accused had earlier sought six weeks to meet their families and were allowed to stay abroad till Oct 23. They were arrested on March 13 for allegedly training the insurgent-linked groups in Myanmar.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/arms-training-case-us-mercenary-vandyke-6-ukrainians-to-remain-abroad-till-feb-24/articleshow/135154247.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/arms-training-case-us-mercenary-vandyke-6-ukrainians-to-remain-abroad-till-feb-24/articleshow/135154247.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:50:07+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135154643,imgsize-37086.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Opposition's 'mock Parliament' to step up fight against SIR &amp; CEC Gyanesh Kumar]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/oppositions-mock-parliament-to-step-up-fight-against-sir-cec-gyanesh-kumar/articleshow/135154248.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154248.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sources said a “mock” gathering depicting an assembly of MPs may take place in the national capital on Oct 28. The event will involve MPs and others, but is unlikely to be a large gathering, given that a massive show of strength to push for the CEC’s resignation is planned at Ramlila Maidan as a “Delhi chalo” rally.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/oppositions-mock-parliament-to-step-up-fight-against-sir-cec-gyanesh-kumar/articleshow/135154248.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/oppositions-mock-parliament-to-step-up-fight-against-sir-cec-gyanesh-kumar/articleshow/135154248.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:45:37+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135154589,imgsize-160956.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Need to unite against divisive forces, tackle new challenges: PM Modi]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/need-to-unite-against-divisive-forces-tackle-new-challenges-pm-modi/articleshow/135154250.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154250.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Inaugurating the Chinmaya Amrit Mahotsav Global Sammelan, he said Swami Chinmayananda set his goals as per issues facing the country at the time and new challenges had emerged in the past few decades. “We must unite society against divisive forces. We must inspire citizens toward self-reliance, and we must connect every individual to vision of a developed India by 2047. For these objectives, we must become more proactive,” he said.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/need-to-unite-against-divisive-forces-tackle-new-challenges-pm-modi/articleshow/135154250.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/need-to-unite-against-divisive-forces-tackle-new-challenges-pm-modi/articleshow/135154250.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:42:30+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135154532,imgsize-67060.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Centre bans reuse of single-use medical devices across hospitals; flags recycling of disposables]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-bans-reuse-of-single-use-medical-devices-across-hospitals-flags-recycling-of-disposables/articleshow/135154254.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154254.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a letter dated Oct 16, the Directorate General of Health Services (DGHS) said it had come to its notice that some private and corporate hospitals were reusing single-use devices after sterilising them, including items used in cardiology, nephrology, oncology, cardiothoracic and vascular surgery (CTVS), neurosurgery and other clinical services. The DGHS said that reuse could expose patients to cross-infection, device malfunction, reduced performance and other complications.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-bans-reuse-of-single-use-medical-devices-across-hospitals-flags-recycling-of-disposables/articleshow/135154254.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-bans-reuse-of-single-use-medical-devices-across-hospitals-flags-recycling-of-disposables/articleshow/135154254.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:37:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator 